{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For you have mocked me.</b> It would have been fitting for Balaam to marvel at this great wonder of the she-ass's speech, and to be shaken by the unprecedented miracle that dismayed all who traveled with him on the way. He should have thought and reflected that this was from HaShem — to confound his counsel and turn his wisdom backward. But out of his cruelty, the evil of his nature, and his overpowering desire to go, he took the matter in a commonplace way, and therefore he replied as a man speaking with his companion: 'for you have mocked me.' As for the princes of Moab and his two youths who saw this wonder yet asked him nothing and said no word — it is possible to say that they were all ahead of him on the road, and while he remained alone behind, this miracle happened to him, and they did not see it because they were not in the same place. Or perhaps they were all in the same place, yet none saw and heard but Balaam alone, for so it happens to men of the holy spirit, in the manner of what is written concerning Daniel (Daniel 10:7): ״וראיתי אני דניאל לבדי את המראה והאנשים אשר היו עמי לא ראו את המראה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:09.299221389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}